Language: en

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.740 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  ninja Lars gum centric approach to  combat isn't like anything you've played  before so it's understandable to feel a  bit overwhelmed the first time you  attempt a battle royale before you jump  into combat take heed of our guide to  ninja lar fundamentals and you'll be  well on your way to maxing out your s  energy and scoring major it pawns  against the competition fact ninja hates  staying grounded sure they can do it but  they'd much prefer to be running up and  along walls and dashing from rooftop to  rooftop ninja lar knows this all too  well and provides its kitty ninja cast  with huge multi-layered playgrounds  where they can run riot there's  absolutely nothing wrong with using your  first few games simply to get your  bearings and to better acquaint yourself  with navigating the environments using  all the tricks at your disposal  fortunately getting around is extremely  easy just running into walls is enough  for you to get vertical and you'll soon  get the hang of double jumping and using  the dodge to zip around quickly you've  also got the gum - which costs valuable  s energy but allows you to travel huge  distances in a heartbeat you should also  keep an eye out for bubble gum slides  long stretches of gum that you can jump  on to grind between buildings to go  farther even faster if you find that the  default settings are a little too  unorthodox and want something closer to  a traditional action game head to the  control settings and give type D a try  at launch ninjalah features 12 weapons  divided across three categories katanas  are all rounders hammers are slow and  smashy and yo-yos trade power for  striking range once you've picked a type  that broadly suits your style it's time  to dig deeper into the abilities of each  weapon because while standard attacks  are the same across weapons at the same  time they each offer a different mix of  special abilities the one you'll likely  use most in moment-to-moment combat is  gun shoot which is the projectile you  create when blowing a bubble for the  upon katana it's a single hit bubble  that fires off in a straight line while  the skate hammer creates a gun web that  causes chip damage to anyone unfortunate  enough to touch it specials are stronger  attacks managed by a cool-down system  and will trigger a state change on hit  such as a stun knock back or knock down  some like the skate hammers power Buster  have a big and very obvious wind-up but  deal huge damage while others are useful  for closing the gap in an instance such  as the yo-yos yoyo leap the final  consideration is gum ninjutsu the most  powerful attack in a ninjas arsenal the  ninjutsu gauge automatically fills at a  slow pace but can be accelerated by  landing hits once full you're on the  path to an almost guaranteed upon  possibly more than one if you play your  gun right again these vary wildly  between weapon types from devastating  gum tornados to long-range gum beams  that can pass through walls it's also  worth noting that weapons have inherent  abilities ranging from temporary super  armor after an upon to resetting the  cooldown gauge for your special if you  can avoid damage long enough the only  way to truly figure out which weapon  class and type suits you is through  experimentation but even then aim to be  as flexible and adaptable as you can  what might work best as a lone wolf in a  battle royale might not be what's best  for the group in a team battle  s energy or shinobi energy is the power  a ninja requires to perform critical  moves boost their abilities and most  importantly craft big weapons in a nod  to MOBAs your best move at the start of  a round isn't a head straight for your  rivals but rather to track down drones  and destroy them to boost your s energy  capacity from its default four units up  to a maximum of ten if you're feeling  particularly sneaky it's possible to gun  morph close to a drone let a rival do  all the hard work and then steal the  killer blow the s energy bar sits just  below your health but you can also get a  good idea of your status from the size  of the bubble you blow when holding Z L  if you're at six units your bubble will  be bigger and your air dashes will be  faster and at eight units and above your  global will be huge and you'll get a  prompt to create a bigger weapon having  more units also increases the number of  dodges and gun dashes you can perform in  succession the former costing one unit  and dash is costing three also note that  in team battle mode green drones have an  area of effect benefit so any nearby  teammates will also earn the same boost  to their s energy meter in short aim to  be the first to max out your s energy if  you want to be the fastest the deadliest  and wield the biggest weapon  ultimately ninjalah is a high school  contest so knowing how to stay top of  the table is essential pretty much  everything you do earns you points at  the lower end of the scoring spectrum  you can net a small amount by collecting  the s energy orbs dotted around the  arena's but it's when you start landing  hits that the points really rack up a  standard drone can net around 300 points  if you land every hit but the larger  tougher drones will earn you over 400  points but swatting down defenseless  drones will only take you so far if you  want to really start raking in the big  figures you'll have to master upon  finishes there's a few scenarios that  result in an upon the simplest way is to  ko someone with the gum ninjutsu but  they're achievable in standard combat -  if you first bind an opponent in gum  either by hitting them with a gum shoot  or crushing their gum guard with what's  known as a gum break then finish them  with a combo that also does the trick  you'll also get an opportunity if you  win a parry that's where two identical  attacks meet and trigger a showdown  that's akin to a rapid-fire game of  stone Paper Scissors using the left  stick try to remember that up beats down  down beat sideways and sideways beats up  when that follow up with a KO worthy  combo and you'll bag yourself an eight  pond if you both pick the same direction  you'll have to choose again until one of  you wins out and earns a nice bonus in  the process it's also possible to  trigger a parry by using an S burst  while you're being combo'd but this  takes up five units of s energy one  final crucial thing to be aware of is  that the game tracked the number of  drone takedowns and it pawns executed  during a match and awards big bonus  points to the best performers at the  results screen 504 the top drone  destroyer and 1,000 for the it pond  master that's enough to cause major  last-second upsets so try not to slack  on either front the final elements of  building your ultimate gun wielding  ninja is shinobi cards these are  unlocked using the ninja medals you earn  from online play and grant a variety of  enhancements such as the ability to  absorb an opponent's energy see the  position of drones through walls and say  when opponents are behind you cards must  be allocated to a slot to be activated  you'll have one to begin with but ninja  medals can also be spent to open up a  total of four slots shinobi cards also  have a points cost and as a cost cap to  prevent you from becoming opie although  that cap increases the more card slots  you have open each card also has a set  of three sub skills called assist codes  which are both unlockable and  upgradeable with you guessed it ninja  medals it's important to note that  shinobi cards cannot be acquired using  the purchasable currency jolla in order  to avoid a pay to win scenario think of  shinobi cards as a means of either  making your character even stronger as  an aspect of combat you're already  proficient in or a solution to  addressing a weakness in your skill set  with four slots opened up you'll have an  even greater opportunity to mix and  match your optimal setup hopefully this  short guide has armed you with the  knowledge you need to get out there and  show the world who's truly the world's  mightiest ninja and if you haven't  gotten in July yet don't forget that  it's exclusive to Nintendo switch and is  truly free-to-play you don't even need a  Nintendo online subscription to join the  fight

